ists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-01T05:13:36Z","updated_at":"2025-10-01T05:16:06Z","body":"Also be aware that instead of e.g. exchanging `CMP_EPSILON`, the correct thing to do in some situations with small delta is simply to do nothing at all (preferably as high up in the call chain as possible).\r\n\r\nThen maybe add a `DEV_ASSERT()` and a note further down that a zero is not expected.\r\n\r\n(Just to note I haven't checked these in detail, they may be fine as they are, it's just a general note.)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3354772050/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]